# Keep the deploy to what the site actually loads.
#
# js/film.js picks its frame directory at runtime:
#   const FRAME_DIR = PHONE ? "dive-720" : "dive";
# so `dive/` (42MB) and `dive-720/` (9.5MB) are the ONLY frame sets that ship.
# Everything below is a superseded export kept locally as a backup — together
# they are ~140MB of dead weight that would otherwise be uploaded on every
# deploy and served from the edge for no reason.

assets/hero/frames-4k/
assets/hero/frames-25mb/
assets/hero/frames-v2-backup/
assets/hero/frames-v3-720p/
assets/hero/frames-v3-backup/

# Unreferenced stills (15.7MB). Grep of index.html, js/ and *.css finds no
# use of either; they are source plates for the frame renders.
assets/hero/shot-a-hunter.png
assets/hero/shot-b-eye.png

# Netlify/Cloudflare cache-header format. Vercel does not read this file —
# the policy it describes now lives in vercel.json. Kept in the repo for the
# other hosts, excluded here so it cannot imply it is doing something.
_headers

# Local noise
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.claude/
reference/
BRIEF.md
